    description: "Per session_retrospective_05012026_1810.md Finding 2: on May 1 the user asked 'Are ADR 25 and 26 playbooks masquerading as ADRs?' and 'are there any other (older) ADRs masquerading as audit-findings documents?'. There is currently no playbook that routes between document types — ADR vs audit-findings vs lab-notebook vs playbook vs tracker-item. The Fundamental Concept Audit playbook produces *findings* but doesn't say where to file them; the ADR README is the only doc-type spec and doesn't define neighbors. Proposed: add a doc-type routing playbook (or a §Doc-types section in docs/adr/README.md) enumerating each type's purpose, distinguishing markers, and lifecycle. Reference it from the Fundamental Concept Audit playbook §Step 6 and from AGENTS.md §Required-Checks → Fundamental Concept Audit. Note: the user separately filed an item to 'auditize' ADRs 25 and 26 and revise prompting around ADR-vs-audit-findings — that work and this work are complementary; consider parenting or sequencing."  # c4e7
